### Phase 2 implementation record

Phase 1 proved the original single context-menu handler insufficient, so the
conditional no-generalization branch was intentionally not selected. The
implementation follows the required smallest-generalization branch:

- `dwarfuicore/context_menu/input_hook.lua` remains the sole native and
  Lua-screen trampoline owner. It now has a fixed private order represented by
  the immutable numeric `InputConsumerKind`: one injected priority consumer,
  followed by one context-menu adapter, followed by the exact predecessor.
  There is no registration API, arbitrary priority list, fullscreen screen, or
  UserPrompt-specific lifecycle code.
- `prepare_priority_consumer(root, consumer)` validates and copies the stand-in
  callbacks and performs the fallible native or Lua-screen seam preparation.
  It publishes one exact prepared token. `activate_priority_consumer(token)`
  accepts only that token and commits through non-throwing assignments without
  rewrapping. `release_priority_consumer(token)` clears prepared or active
  ownership first and performs idempotent best-effort root rollback.
- Priority ownership classification occurs before protected handling. Once an
  event is classified as owned, handler failure or a non-boolean result is
  reported to the injected `on_failure` observer and returns true without
  calling context-menu or base-game code. Failure before ownership is known is
  reported and delegates. Exact false continues to the next consumer; exact
  true stops dispatch. Context-menu failure retains its characterized
  transparent delegation and generation disablement.
- Context-menu root demand is copied into a weak set and reconciled with an
  active priority root, retaining one native trampoline and weak Lua-screen
  records. Foreign outer wrappers, exact predecessor returns, root retirement,
  same-generation module adoption, and inert retired trampolines retain their
  established behavior.
- `context_menu/service.lua` is reduced to the intentional
  `set_context_consumer(handler, failure_handler)` adapter. It still owns normal
  right-click opening behavior while no priority consumer handles the event.
- Explicit reload still retires the full context-menu service first. If only a
  partial registration/input graph was loaded, `dwarfuicore/command.lua` now
  retires both the registration manager and the input dispatcher; a fully
  loaded service prevents duplicate input shutdown.
- Registry order and package inventory remain unchanged because no module was
  added or moved. The registry still loads the one input owner before the
  renderer and context-menu service. Package tests inspect every registered
  production module and prove only `context_menu/input_hook.lua` references the
  native input seam and no `user_prompt/input_hook.lua` exists.

Actual Phase 2 files are limited to:

- production: `dwarfuicore/context_menu/input_hook.lua`,
  `dwarfuicore/context_menu/service.lua`, and `dwarfuicore/command.lua`;
- focused units: `tests/context_menu/input_hook.spec.lua`,
  `tests/context_menu/service.spec.lua`, `tests/dwarfuicore_command.spec.lua`,
  and `tests/package_contract.spec.lua`; and
- this execution record.

No proposal, installed mod, sibling repository, provider API, tooltip module,
new UserPrompt module, or context-menu registration/definition was changed.

